# Prettier reads .gitignore too, so build output and node_modules need no line here.
#
# Everything below has a writer other than a person, and that writer's next run would undo a
# reformat here and show every reformatted line in its diff.

# `pnpm types:cms`.
server/payload-types.ts

# `pnpm sync:translations`.
lib/translations.en.json

pnpm-lock.yaml

# `pnpm redirects:generate` and its snapshot commands (#276), named before they reach main so that
# PR needs no edit here. Its `build.test.ts` compares the map with the generator's output.
lib/legacy-redirects/map.generated.json
data/legacy-redirects/

# Copies from sydevs/claude-workflow. `audit-contracts` checks the rule's canonical block against
# claude-workflow's docs/code-comments.md; the workflow is that repo's own file, kept alike in
# every sydevs repo.
docs/rules/code-comments.md
.github/workflows/workflow-state.yml

# Claude Code's Protected Paths guard holds every write here for approval (AGENTS.md), so a
# repo-wide `prettier --write` would stall an unattended run.
.claude/

# Markdown is written by people, but Prettier rewrites a fenced tsx sample as a statement
# (`;<Icon … />`, a JSX attribute as `className = '…'`) and pads every table. Nothing checks
# Markdown formatting: ESLint's prettier rule covers only the files ESLint lints.
*.md
